+# CatPack 0.9.0
+
+## Before you run it: two Firebase steps
+
+1. **Publish the security rules.** Firebase console → Firestore Database → Rules → paste [`firestore.rules`](firestore.rules) → Publish (or `firebase deploy --only firestore:rules` from the repo root).
+2. **Flag your coaches.** Firestore Database → Data → `users` → the coach's uid → set `role` to `coach` (string). Everyone else stays `athlete`. The app can't change roles.
+
+## What changed
+
+| Request | What it does now |
+|---|---|
+| Dark and light mode, no Graphite | Account & settings → Appearance: System default / Light / Dark. Blue & Gold became Dark, Daylight became Light, Graphite is gone. Saved Graphite or Blue & Gold choices open as Dark. |
+| Log tab has every Workouts-tab exercise, plus add | The exercise field opens a searchable list of every exercise from the editor suggestions, premade workouts and sport plans, plus your saved workouts and your own. Typing a name that isn't there offers "Add". Custom exercises sync with your account and show up in the workout editor and on the Leaderboard. |
+| No heaviest-set line | The chart shows only the best estimated max per day. |
+| Log whole workouts under the graph, with dates and check-offs | Workout log card under the chart: Log workout (or the new Log button on any workout card) → pick the day → checklist. Grouped by month, newest or oldest first, filter All / To finish / Done. In a workout: tap to check off, Log set records the weight on the chart for that day, change the date, add or remove exercises, mark all done, delete. |
+| Team select screen, join and create teams, codes | After signing in: your teams, General use, Join a team (code), Create a team (coaches only). Codes are 8 letters and numbers (about 850 billion possibilities), only the creator can see them again (Settings → Team code), and they can be reset. |
+| General leaderboard of everyone using General | In General use the Leaderboard ranks everyone else using the app on their own (top 100 per exercise), unless they turn it off in Account & settings. |
+| Non-coaches can add only one athlete | Athlete accounts have one athlete, themselves, made automatically from their account (see below): one per team and one in General use. Enforced by the security rules, not just the app. |
+| Sign-up makes the athlete | Create account asks for name, email and password (required) and position, body weight and phone (optional). Opening a team or General use makes your athlete profile there from those, so nobody adds themselves. Editing your profile (Account & settings → pencil, or Edit on your own athlete) updates your account and your athlete on every team. Coaches get one automatically in General use but not on teams (so they aren't on their own roster); they can add themselves there by hand. Google sign-ups start with just a name and can fill in the rest in Account & settings. |
+| Account & settings (tap your profile picture) | Its own page, not a tab. Profile (photo, name, role, position, body weight, phone), team (switch, code, members, leave), appearance, privacy (General leaderboard, initials, photo, teammates seeing your progress), your exercises, copy pre-0.9 lifts from this phone, change password, sign out, delete account. |
+| Switch team button | In the header under the app name (shows the open team), and in Account & settings. |
+| Profile pictures | Pick from the phone's photos (no permission needed). Shown in the header, Account & settings, team select and leaderboard rows. Stored as a small JPEG in Firestore, so no paid Cloud Storage bucket is needed. |
+
+Also fixed: the chart line and the 1st-place badge were drawn in `colorOnPrimary`, which made them invisible in light mode (both were on the known-bugs list).
+
+## Data
+
+Athletes, sets and workout logs moved from the phone (Room) to Cloud Firestore, so teammates see the same data. Each team (and each person's General space) has its own data. The workout library stays on the phone. Athletes and sets saved by 0.8 aren't deleted: the app offers once to copy them into the open team or General, and Settings can do it any time.
+
+## Checked here
+
+- All 54 JVM unit tests pass (the existing ones plus new tests for leaderboards, best sets, the exercise list, join codes and the workout log).
+- The whole app type-checks with Kotlin 2.2 against stubs of the Android, Material, Firebase and chart APIs, with ViewBinding and `R` generated from the real layouts (this harness also caught deliberately planted errors).
+- Every resource reference in the XML resolves; the new icons were rendered and checked.
+
+Not checked here: a real Gradle build, the app on a device, and the rules in the Firebase emulator (this workspace couldn't reach Google's Maven or Gradle servers). Run `.\gradlew.bat assembleDebug` and `.\gradlew.bat :app:testDebugUnitTest` first.
